1
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:09,980
Have you ever thought about me?

2
00:00:10,360 --> 00:00:11,220
You can do whatever you want,

3
00:00:11,240 --> 00:00:12,630
but I can't.

4
00:00:14,230 --> 00:00:15,000
Fight.

5
00:00:15,460 --> 00:00:16,970
You don't know anything

6
00:00:17,430 --> 00:00:18,530
about us or my training.

7
00:00:19,970 --> 00:00:20,710
Whoa...

8
00:00:29,930 --> 00:00:31,090
I trusted you with this.

9
00:00:31,110 --> 00:00:32,509
What the hell have you done?

10
00:00:32,910 --> 00:00:34,730
P'Ing, I didn't do it.

11
00:00:49,630 --> 00:00:51,010
Dammit, Yok.

12
00:00:57,250 --> 00:00:59,310
That boxer hits like a damn truck.

13
00:01:02,890 --> 00:01:03,760
Dammit.

14
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:10,210
Jeez.

15
00:01:12,310 --> 00:01:13,470
God, what the hell?

16
00:01:17,650 --> 00:01:18,570
Who is it?

17
00:01:20,090 --> 00:01:20,840
Mr. Phet?

18
00:01:23,310 --> 00:01:24,210
Hello, Mr. Phet.

19
00:01:24,490 --> 00:01:25,650
Hello, Mr. Ing.

20
00:01:25,670 --> 00:01:27,120
My family went out for a meal yesterday,

21
00:01:27,150 --> 00:01:28,910
and the staff at the restaurant told me what happened.

22
00:01:28,930 --> 00:01:31,150
-I'm really sorry for what Yok did. -Oh.

23
00:01:31,539 --> 00:01:32,860
Is that all it was?

24
00:01:32,940 --> 00:01:34,690
I don't mind at all.

25
00:01:35,120 --> 00:01:36,229
I've told him to apologize to you

26
00:01:36,259 --> 00:01:37,440
in person at your house.

27
00:01:38,289 --> 00:01:39,710
Oh, come on.

28
00:01:39,910 --> 00:01:42,539
You're worrying too much.

29
00:01:43,100 --> 00:01:44,770
Oh, so Yok is on his way?

30
00:01:45,009 --> 00:01:46,770
Alright, I'll wait for him.

31
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:48,289
I'm really sorry, Mr. Ing.

32
00:01:48,490 --> 00:01:49,479
Thank you very much.

33
00:01:51,630 --> 00:01:54,620
Finally, someone has managed to tame him.

34
00:02:00,020 --> 00:02:01,350
Whoa.

35
00:02:04,120 --> 00:02:05,750
Didn't take you long, kid.

36
00:02:16,660 --> 00:02:18,530
You said you were done with me,

37
00:02:18,700 --> 00:02:20,870
yet here you are, dragging yourself all the way here.

38
00:02:21,810 --> 00:02:22,860
I'm here to apologize.

39
00:02:24,490 --> 00:02:25,320
Apologize?

40
00:02:32,130 --> 00:02:32,930
Seriously?

41
00:02:33,720 --> 00:02:35,160
Is that how you apologize?

42
00:02:36,300 --> 00:02:37,390
I'm sorry.

43
00:02:38,890 --> 00:02:40,650
I planned to just drop these off

44
00:02:40,680 --> 00:02:41,660
and then call you.

45
00:02:42,600 --> 00:02:44,670
But since you're here anyway,

46
00:02:44,910 --> 00:02:46,210
I'll say it to your face.

47
00:02:46,620 --> 00:02:47,540
I'm sorry.

48
00:02:49,090 --> 00:02:49,970
I mean,

49
00:02:50,390 --> 00:02:52,010
I thought you'd be out on a date,

50
00:02:53,220 --> 00:02:54,520
so I didn't want to bother you.

51
00:02:57,400 --> 00:02:58,350
I told you last time.

52
00:02:58,380 --> 00:03:00,020
If you're jealous, just say so.

53
00:03:01,190 --> 00:03:02,460
I can explain.

54
00:03:09,250 --> 00:03:10,160
Here.

55
00:03:12,740 --> 00:03:13,460
I'm off.

56
00:03:15,020 --> 00:03:16,220
Hey, hold on.

57
00:03:25,090 --> 00:03:26,420
Make me some shrimp porridge.

58
00:03:30,100 --> 00:03:32,090
And are you going to pour it over my head again?

59
00:03:37,230 --> 00:03:37,930
Have you been nice

60
00:03:37,950 --> 00:03:39,840
enough for me to be nice to you?

61
00:03:42,829 --> 00:03:44,720
Suit yourself. If you don't wanna do it, fine.

62
00:03:45,250 --> 00:03:46,990
I'll just send all this trash

63
00:03:47,150 --> 00:03:49,680
straight to your brother, okay?

64
00:03:52,280 --> 00:03:53,180
Suit yourself.

65
00:03:53,210 --> 00:03:54,520
Wait, hold on.

66
00:03:57,829 --> 00:03:59,170
If I make it, we're done, right?

67
00:04:31,340 --> 00:04:32,490
Yeah, fine.

68
00:04:33,020 --> 00:04:34,400
I guess I can forgive you.

69
00:04:37,159 --> 00:04:38,430
I'm free next week.

70
00:04:38,590 --> 00:04:40,230
I'm taking two people from the agriculture company

71
00:04:40,250 --> 00:04:41,500
to visit the site in Pattaya.

72
00:04:43,970 --> 00:04:45,230
Your brother is coming, too.

73
00:04:45,740 --> 00:04:47,150
Are you okay with the date?

74
00:04:49,850 --> 00:04:50,600
Yes.

75
00:05:26,340 --> 00:05:27,350
This is terrible.

76
00:05:48,300 --> 00:05:51,430
♪ Love me so much it hurts, ♪

77
00:05:52,430 --> 00:05:55,390
♪ But you never let it show ♪

78
00:05:56,700 --> 00:05:58,940
♪ Choosing silence, you'd never let me know ♪

79
00:06:01,650 --> 00:06:04,530
♪ Oh, oh ♪

80
00:06:05,670 --> 00:06:08,870
♪ How many endings can love hold? ♪

81
00:06:10,130 --> 00:06:12,240
♪ Only one, the same old ♪

82
00:06:14,880 --> 00:06:16,130
♪ Wake up all the night ♪

83
00:06:16,160 --> 00:06:17,400
♪ Stay out of matter ♪

84
00:06:17,420 --> 00:06:18,940
♪ Maybe it won't hurt as much ♪

85
00:06:18,970 --> 00:06:22,980
♪ If I just sleep the day away ♪

86
00:06:26,420 --> 00:06:28,800
♪ I think you're like a masterpiece, ♪

87
00:06:28,830 --> 00:06:30,550
♪ But I mess it up ♪

88
00:06:30,590 --> 00:06:33,480
♪ Don't wanna walk a step behind it ♪

89
00:06:33,860 --> 00:06:35,310
♪ A step behind you ♪

90
00:06:36,950 --> 00:06:38,580
♪ A step behind you ♪

91
00:07:08,850 --> 00:07:11,900
♪ I'm always a step behind ♪

92
00:07:11,980 --> 00:07:15,260
♪ I'm always a step behind ♪

93
00:07:18,580 --> 00:07:21,880
♪ I think you're like a masterpiece, ♪

94
00:07:21,900 --> 00:07:23,460
♪ But I mess it up ♪

95
00:07:23,540 --> 00:07:26,470
♪ Don't wanna walk a step behind it ♪

96
00:07:26,900 --> 00:07:28,540
♪ A step behind you ♪

97
00:07:29,310 --> 00:07:31,840
♪ I'm always a step behind ♪

98
00:07:34,270 --> 00:07:35,659
♪ Love me... ♪

99
00:07:51,940 --> 00:07:52,760
Jeez.

100
00:07:53,300 --> 00:07:55,270
I've been practicing for so long.

101
00:07:56,300 --> 00:07:58,090
Thought I'd be able to hold you back.

102
00:08:01,700 --> 00:08:03,160
You'll surpass me in no time.

103
00:08:03,520 --> 00:08:05,010
I won't be playing much anymore.

104
00:08:07,200 --> 00:08:08,000
Why not?

105
00:08:09,840 --> 00:08:11,240
I passed the tryouts.

106
00:08:13,060 --> 00:08:14,600
I have to sign a contract and go to America.

107
00:08:16,240 --> 00:08:18,090
Once I become a professional boxer,

108
00:08:18,200 --> 00:08:19,540
I won't have much time for this.

109
00:08:20,210 --> 00:08:22,180
Hey, congratulations.

110
00:08:23,120 --> 00:08:24,270
But...

111
00:08:26,200 --> 00:08:27,550
you're not running away

112
00:08:29,500 --> 00:08:31,170
just because you fell for my brother, are you?

113
00:08:35,970 --> 00:08:36,789
No.

114
00:08:37,190 --> 00:08:38,220
What are you talking about?

115
00:08:41,320 --> 00:08:43,100
That was rude, you know.

116
00:08:44,380 --> 00:08:45,780
Well, since you're leaving,

117
00:08:46,050 --> 00:08:47,590
I just wanted to tease you.

118
00:08:53,040 --> 00:08:53,940
Another round?

119
00:09:12,680 --> 00:09:14,090
What's your take on this project?

120
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:16,680
It's not worth investing in yet.

121
00:09:16,880 --> 00:09:18,540
They have control over all the key technology,

122
00:09:18,570 --> 00:09:19,580
which puts us in a weak position.

123
00:09:21,020 --> 00:09:21,940
Keep going.

124
00:09:22,610 --> 00:09:23,770
We should let them

125
00:09:23,790 --> 00:09:25,220
apply for the license first,

126
00:09:25,250 --> 00:09:26,500
then decide what to do next.

127
00:09:29,040 --> 00:09:30,200
Good read on the situation.

128
00:09:31,360 --> 00:09:33,560
You'll be in charge of this project,

129
00:09:34,110 --> 00:09:36,190
so do your homework and make sure you seal the deal.

130
00:09:38,260 --> 00:09:39,160
Understood.

131
00:09:53,520 --> 00:09:56,500
If that's settled, let's proceed as we agreed.

132
00:09:56,820 --> 00:09:57,680
Cheers.

133
00:10:03,770 --> 00:10:04,850
Well...

134
00:10:06,920 --> 00:10:09,820
we found that some of the documents are still incomplete,

135
00:10:10,420 --> 00:10:13,140
so we'd like to push it back for another two days.

136
00:10:13,330 --> 00:10:16,820
That would be for the best.

137
00:10:17,640 --> 00:10:18,650
Oh, I see.

138
00:10:19,580 --> 00:10:20,980
Well, Mr. Phet.

139
00:10:22,880 --> 00:10:24,960
Can we reschedule the meeting with them?

140
00:10:32,800 --> 00:10:34,530
If they're having technical issues,

141
00:10:34,840 --> 00:10:37,920
we should give them some time.

142
00:10:42,520 --> 00:10:43,970
In that case, Mr. Phet,

143
00:10:44,220 --> 00:10:44,870
if possible,

144
00:10:44,890 --> 00:10:47,340
could we make it this Thursday or Friday?

145
00:10:47,360 --> 00:10:48,680
I have to go to Samui on Saturday.

146
00:10:49,220 --> 00:10:50,100
Of course.

147
00:10:50,810 --> 00:10:53,560
We'll get everything sorted out as soon as possible.

148
00:10:56,920 --> 00:10:57,950
Thank you very much.

149
00:10:59,650 --> 00:11:01,400
Now, let's eat.

150
00:11:02,620 --> 00:11:03,850
-Yes. -Sure.

151
00:11:06,940 --> 00:11:07,810
Want some shrimp?

152
00:11:08,860 --> 00:11:09,690
No, thanks.

153
00:11:26,740 --> 00:11:27,680
-Alright. -What do you think?

154
00:11:48,880 --> 00:11:50,180
The location is quite promising.

155
00:11:50,300 --> 00:11:52,140
I'll need everyone to prepare the documents

156
00:11:52,160 --> 00:11:53,590
and follow through with the plan.

157
00:11:53,620 --> 00:11:55,600
Let's meet up again in a month.

158
00:11:56,150 --> 00:11:58,960
That'll give Mr. Phet time to persuade the others

159
00:11:58,980 --> 00:11:59,980
to join the project.

160
00:12:01,060 --> 00:12:03,740
No problem at all. You can count on us.

161
00:12:04,330 --> 00:12:05,740
Alright then, goodbye.

162
00:12:06,440 --> 00:12:07,260
Goodbye.

163
00:12:13,780 --> 00:12:14,500
Wait.

164
00:12:27,330 --> 00:12:28,130
Samui?

165
00:12:32,900 --> 00:12:34,900
Secretary Piang said the tickets are non-refundable.

166
00:12:35,400 --> 00:12:36,630
If you want to come, then come.

167
00:12:37,140 --> 00:12:38,430
I won't force you if you don't want to.

168
00:12:55,140 --> 00:12:55,800
Okay.

169
00:13:02,860 --> 00:13:05,100
Why should I have to beg him?

170
00:13:10,420 --> 00:13:11,600
Mr. Ing, I'll keep you updated.

171
00:13:11,620 --> 00:13:12,500
Got it.

172
00:13:46,850 --> 00:13:48,630
Hello.

173
00:13:52,500 --> 00:13:54,500
You've come at the wrong time, sir.

174
00:13:54,610 --> 00:13:56,450
A storm has just decided to roll in.

175
00:13:58,280 --> 00:13:59,740
I'm leaving in two days.

176
00:14:00,150 --> 00:14:01,920
Can we even do a site visit in this weather?

177
00:14:02,340 --> 00:14:04,600
If the rain lets up tomorrow, it's still possible.

178
00:14:04,950 --> 00:14:06,100
Even though construction has halted,

179
00:14:06,120 --> 00:14:07,850
we can still inspect the site.

180
00:14:09,380 --> 00:14:10,820
Let's play it by ear tomorrow.

181
00:14:11,240 --> 00:14:11,930
Yes, sir.

182
00:14:12,700 --> 00:14:14,530
Then, please head to your rooms and get some rest,

183
00:14:14,550 --> 00:14:16,140
both you and your assistant.

184
00:14:33,890 --> 00:14:36,050
What's with all this damn rain?

185
00:14:41,910 --> 00:14:43,440
Don't be rude, sweetie.

186
00:14:43,530 --> 00:14:45,130
Apologize to him now.

187
00:14:45,670 --> 00:14:46,600
I'm sorry.

188
00:14:46,630 --> 00:14:47,600
Oh, it's fine.

189
00:14:47,810 --> 00:14:48,990
Let him have his fun.

190
00:14:49,130 --> 00:14:50,440
Are you swimming all by yourself?

191
00:14:51,020 --> 00:14:52,780
Want me to keep you company?

192
00:15:04,030 --> 00:15:05,040
That was a direct hit.

193
00:15:10,240 --> 00:15:11,580
It must be nice being kids.

194
00:15:11,890 --> 00:15:14,500
They can still have fun no matter how bad the storm is.

195
00:15:16,100 --> 00:15:17,600
Sure, the kids have fun,

196
00:15:17,830 --> 00:15:21,140
but the parents are stuck and can't go anywhere,

197
00:15:21,270 --> 00:15:22,890
having to keep an eye on them.

198
00:15:24,060 --> 00:15:24,930
I know.

199
00:15:28,250 --> 00:15:29,650
I've found him.

200
00:15:32,850 --> 00:15:34,930
I have to keep an eye on him all day and night.

201
00:15:40,390 --> 00:15:41,270
Leaving already?

202
00:15:42,620 --> 00:15:45,720
You certainly know how to look for pleasure, don't you?

203
00:15:46,660 --> 00:15:48,380
Is this your friend?

204
00:15:48,770 --> 00:15:49,500
Yes,

205
00:15:49,810 --> 00:15:50,620
he is.

206
00:16:02,960 --> 00:16:04,650
Is it that unbearable

207
00:16:04,670 --> 00:16:05,980
to sleep alone for just one night?

208
00:16:06,880 --> 00:16:07,930
What is your problem?

209
00:16:10,310 --> 00:16:11,220
The second we arrive,

210
00:16:11,250 --> 00:16:13,920
you're sitting here laughing with a stranger.

211
00:16:14,460 --> 00:16:15,530
Aren't you afraid at all?

212
00:16:20,450 --> 00:16:21,130
What's so funny?

213
00:16:24,080 --> 00:16:25,410
I've been wondering

214
00:16:25,430 --> 00:16:27,680
why you made such a scene at Leo's place.

215
00:16:27,880 --> 00:16:29,310
I finally get it.

216
00:16:29,800 --> 00:16:31,660
You just don't understand your own feelings.

217
00:16:32,090 --> 00:16:33,420
When I was chasing you,

218
00:16:33,610 --> 00:16:34,740
you ignored me.

219
00:16:34,760 --> 00:16:36,460
But now that I've stopped, you're upset.

220
00:16:36,590 --> 00:16:39,060
Do you realize you're being such a psycho?

221
00:16:39,280 --> 00:16:40,290
You always need someone

222
00:16:40,310 --> 00:16:42,700
running after you.

223
00:16:47,320 --> 00:16:49,140
I already told you, I'm not jealous of you.

224
00:16:49,170 --> 00:16:50,780
-You're so full of yourself. -Yeah, fine.

225
00:16:50,830 --> 00:16:52,340
Whatever. Think what you want.

226
00:16:52,370 --> 00:16:53,480
I don't care anymore

227
00:16:53,600 --> 00:16:54,530
because I'm not gonna commit

228
00:16:54,550 --> 00:16:56,120
to just you.

229
00:16:56,150 --> 00:16:57,450
I'm going to have my own fun, okay?

230
00:16:58,000 --> 00:16:58,740
P'Ing,

231
00:16:59,220 --> 00:17:00,480
we need to sort this out first.

232
00:17:02,240 --> 00:17:04,079
We're in public, you know.

233
00:17:25,800 --> 00:17:27,530
You know why this suits you?

234
00:17:27,550 --> 00:17:28,740
Let me tell you something.

235
00:17:29,950 --> 00:17:31,300
Just take this.

236
00:17:31,320 --> 00:17:32,930
Open your damn eyes and look.

237
00:17:33,240 --> 00:17:34,340
He's here with his son.

238
00:17:37,690 --> 00:17:38,700
Look at me.

239
00:17:39,280 --> 00:17:40,330
You idiot.

240
00:18:22,180 --> 00:18:24,640
Mr. Ing, we only have half a day.

241
00:18:24,660 --> 00:18:26,970
Any later and the rain will start pouring down again.

242
00:18:27,030 --> 00:18:28,170
Alright, let's go.

243
00:18:28,190 --> 00:18:29,250
Hello, Mr. Ing.

244
00:18:31,560 --> 00:18:32,290
Which way?

245
00:18:32,310 --> 00:18:33,490
-This way, please. -Right this way.

246
00:18:55,280 --> 00:18:56,380
This way, please.

247
00:19:05,320 --> 00:19:06,250
Since it's right by the sea,

248
00:19:06,280 --> 00:19:08,200
you have to be extra careful with the paint.

249
00:19:09,770 --> 00:19:11,580
Because if a problem arises later,

250
00:19:11,610 --> 00:19:12,900
it'll be a nightmare to fix.

251
00:19:14,040 --> 00:19:16,100
The materials we're using are top-grade

252
00:19:16,120 --> 00:19:17,230
and guaranteed to be moisture-resistant

253
00:19:17,260 --> 00:19:18,570
and insect-proof.

254
00:19:18,740 --> 00:19:19,470
I see.

255
00:19:21,330 --> 00:19:22,280
Mr. Ing,

256
00:19:23,460 --> 00:19:25,140
do you have some free time today?

257
00:19:25,210 --> 00:19:27,400
The higher-ups found out you were in town,

258
00:19:27,430 --> 00:19:29,440
so they'd like to invite you to dinner.

259
00:19:30,830 --> 00:19:31,710
How did they find out?

260
00:19:31,740 --> 00:19:33,090
I'm not sure myself.

261
00:19:33,450 --> 00:19:34,950
Since your visit was quite sudden,

262
00:19:34,970 --> 00:19:36,190
we didn't notify anyone.

263
00:19:36,360 --> 00:19:38,720
But for some reason, word has gotten out to everyone.

264
00:19:46,490 --> 00:19:47,580
You should go, Mr. Ing.

265
00:19:47,790 --> 00:19:49,420
I'll handle things here.

266
00:19:53,820 --> 00:19:54,570
Alright.

267
00:19:54,950 --> 00:19:56,240
I'm counting on you, then.

268
00:19:56,480 --> 00:19:58,170
Record everything and send the video to me.

269
00:19:58,380 --> 00:20:00,160
If you have any questions, ask the foreman.

270
00:20:00,940 --> 00:20:01,740
Yes, sir.

271
00:20:07,050 --> 00:20:07,850
You sure you're up for it?

272
00:20:09,340 --> 00:20:10,140
I'm sure.

273
00:20:12,460 --> 00:20:13,860
-This way, please. -Okay.

274
00:20:50,090 --> 00:20:51,830
[Call me when you see this. Need to discuss work.]

275
00:20:51,850 --> 00:20:52,660
[Read]

276
00:20:56,760 --> 00:20:57,940
[Please avoid outdoor activities.]

277
00:20:57,970 --> 00:20:59,400
[A major storm is approaching the island.]

278
00:20:59,420 --> 00:21:00,580
[Residents are advised to stay indoors.]

279
00:21:02,480 --> 00:21:03,280
[Please avoid outdoor activities.]

280
00:21:03,300 --> 00:21:04,230
[A major storm is approaching the island.]

281
00:21:04,250 --> 00:21:04,980
[Residents are advised to stay indoors.]

282
00:21:06,520 --> 00:21:07,040
[Please avoid outdoor activities.]

283
00:21:07,070 --> 00:21:07,740
[A major storm is approaching the island.]

284
00:21:07,760 --> 00:21:08,220
[Residents are advised to stay indoors.]

285
00:21:14,400 --> 00:21:15,200
Yok...

286
00:21:26,280 --> 00:21:27,980
Why the hell isn't he picking up?

287
00:21:32,850 --> 00:21:33,650
Yok.

288
00:21:34,360 --> 00:21:35,160
Yok.

289
00:21:35,740 --> 00:21:36,910
Are you in there?

290
00:21:43,250 --> 00:21:45,620
-P'Ing? -Hey, where are you?

291
00:21:45,650 --> 00:21:47,290
I'm still at the site.

292
00:21:47,610 --> 00:21:49,420
Something hit me in the shoulder.

293
00:21:49,450 --> 00:21:50,890
-What? -It really hurts.

294
00:21:50,910 --> 00:21:52,090
Yok? Hey.

295
00:22:02,800 --> 00:22:03,590
Hello?

296
00:22:04,710 --> 00:22:06,070
My assistant is trapped at the site.

297
00:22:06,090 --> 00:22:08,020
Get the gear ready and get me a car.

298
00:22:21,420 --> 00:22:23,310
Mr. Ing, we've already notified the police.

299
00:22:23,340 --> 00:22:24,370
This is mine, right?

300
00:22:24,410 --> 00:22:26,880
We can wait until the storm passes.

301
00:22:26,910 --> 00:22:28,220
It'll be too late by then.

302
00:22:28,250 --> 00:22:29,050
Mr. Ing...

303
00:22:29,290 --> 00:22:31,610
He's with me. He's my responsibility.

304
00:22:33,240 --> 00:22:34,910
I've never been afraid of anything in my life

305
00:22:35,440 --> 00:22:37,640
except death itself.

306
00:22:37,970 --> 00:22:39,730
That's something determined by fate,

307
00:22:39,750 --> 00:22:40,750
not by us mortals.

308
00:23:04,130 --> 00:23:06,540
[Yok]

309
00:23:09,370 --> 00:23:10,550
Why isn't he picking up?

310
00:23:13,460 --> 00:23:15,370
[Yok]

311
00:23:15,430 --> 00:23:17,220
Yok, I'm on my way.

312
00:23:17,270 --> 00:23:18,080
P'Ing...

313
00:23:18,190 --> 00:23:19,870
Stay on the line. Don't fall asleep.

314
00:23:20,020 --> 00:23:21,060
I'm rushing there.

315
00:23:21,360 --> 00:23:22,240
Don't close your eyes.

316
00:23:22,260 --> 00:23:23,610
It's so cold...

317
00:23:24,700 --> 00:23:25,500
Yok.

318
00:23:28,390 --> 00:23:31,760
The number you are calling cannot be reached at this time.

319
00:24:33,700 --> 00:24:34,590
Yok.

320
00:24:35,870 --> 00:24:36,830
Yok.

321
00:24:41,160 --> 00:24:42,060
Yok.

322
00:24:45,270 --> 00:24:46,150
Yok.

323
00:24:47,550 --> 00:24:48,310
Yok.

324
00:24:59,310 --> 00:25:00,220
Yok...

325
00:25:23,040 --> 00:25:24,020
Yok.

326
00:25:45,060 --> 00:25:46,250
Yok.

327
00:25:54,900 --> 00:25:55,750
Yok.

328
00:26:08,280 --> 00:26:09,490
P'Ing...

329
00:26:10,320 --> 00:26:11,370
Yok.

330
00:26:51,170 --> 00:26:52,200
P'Ing...

331
00:27:13,480 --> 00:27:14,440
P'Ing...

332
00:27:22,030 --> 00:27:22,830
P'Ing...

333
00:27:23,530 --> 00:27:24,330
Yok.

334
00:27:25,670 --> 00:27:26,470
Yok.

335
00:27:28,520 --> 00:27:29,700
Can you hear me?

336
00:27:31,580 --> 00:27:32,710
Which floor are you on?

337
00:27:33,560 --> 00:27:34,360
Yok.

338
00:27:36,790 --> 00:27:37,670
Yok.

339
00:27:40,560 --> 00:27:41,540
P'Ing...

340
00:27:41,690 --> 00:27:42,490
Yok.

341
00:27:43,980 --> 00:27:44,830
Yok.

342
00:27:45,660 --> 00:27:46,880
Can you hear me?

343
00:27:48,880 --> 00:27:49,680
Yok.

344
00:27:52,130 --> 00:27:52,910
Yok.

345
00:27:53,810 --> 00:27:54,740
P'Ing...

346
00:27:55,590 --> 00:27:56,370
Yok?

347
00:27:57,900 --> 00:27:58,680
Yok.

348
00:28:03,100 --> 00:28:03,930
P'Ing...

349
00:28:04,530 --> 00:28:05,190
Yok.

350
00:28:07,840 --> 00:28:08,760
Yok.

351
00:28:09,370 --> 00:28:10,070
Yok...

352
00:28:10,590 --> 00:28:11,270
Yok.

353
00:28:12,160 --> 00:28:12,820
Hey.

354
00:28:19,450 --> 00:28:20,630
You're here...

355
00:28:21,410 --> 00:28:23,090
If you can talk, it means you're not dead yet.

356
00:28:24,020 --> 00:28:25,220
Are you badly hurt anywhere?

357
00:28:28,430 --> 00:28:29,230
Dammit.

358
00:28:29,910 --> 00:28:31,980
We can't leave in this weather.

359
00:28:32,830 --> 00:28:33,600
Hold on a second.

360
00:28:38,600 --> 00:28:39,920
Dammit...

361
00:28:40,910 --> 00:28:41,710
Are you okay?

362
00:28:42,910 --> 00:28:44,160
My phone's not working.

363
00:28:45,360 --> 00:28:46,700
It got wet.

364
00:28:47,910 --> 00:28:48,850
Just a second.

365
00:28:53,820 --> 00:28:54,620
Where is it?

366
00:28:55,650 --> 00:28:56,740
Jeez.

367
00:28:57,710 --> 00:28:58,850
How bad is the pain?

368
00:29:00,900 --> 00:29:02,140
Does it feel like you've broken a bone?

369
00:29:02,890 --> 00:29:03,730
No.

370
00:29:03,990 --> 00:29:04,910
Anywhere else?

371
00:29:05,450 --> 00:29:06,340
Dammit.

372
00:29:07,150 --> 00:29:08,130
On your neck, too.

373
00:29:08,510 --> 00:29:09,690
Hold this for a second.

374
00:29:11,890 --> 00:29:13,030
I need to clean your wounds first.

375
00:29:15,990 --> 00:29:17,990
I've never actually treated wounds before.

376
00:29:21,710 --> 00:29:22,880
Why are you staring at me?

377
00:29:24,440 --> 00:29:25,090
What?

378
00:29:26,240 --> 00:29:27,140
Is something wrong?

379
00:29:28,690 --> 00:29:29,960
You're alright, aren't you?

380
00:29:47,020 --> 00:29:48,280
Yok, I'm telling you now.

381
00:29:48,310 --> 00:29:50,080
I've never done this for anyone else.

382
00:29:50,890 --> 00:29:54,060
So don't blame me if it hurts.

383
00:29:54,520 --> 00:29:55,160
Come here.

384
00:30:03,310 --> 00:30:05,630
Come on, it's my first time doing this.

385
00:30:06,090 --> 00:30:06,990
Just bear with it.

386
00:30:07,440 --> 00:30:08,910
Yeah, wouldn't want it getting infected.

387
00:30:12,690 --> 00:30:13,910
There's another one on your neck, right?

388
00:30:14,470 --> 00:30:15,840
God, it's massive.

389
00:30:19,650 --> 00:30:20,790
Yeah, just hold on.

390
00:30:20,920 --> 00:30:22,340
Yok, hang in there.

391
00:30:23,150 --> 00:30:24,260
I've never done this.

392
00:30:26,380 --> 00:30:27,590
They'll heal in no time.

393
00:30:31,810 --> 00:30:33,080
It hurts me just looking at you.

394
00:30:36,880 --> 00:30:37,770
You'll be fine.

395
00:30:48,790 --> 00:30:49,590
Want more?

396
00:30:52,030 --> 00:30:52,830
Want some more?

397
00:30:53,460 --> 00:30:54,610
That's enough.

398
00:30:55,830 --> 00:30:57,160
I even brought some crackers

399
00:30:57,190 --> 00:30:58,240
to keep you going.

400
00:30:58,830 --> 00:31:00,000
You'd better thank me.

401
00:31:01,110 --> 00:31:03,360
Guys like me don't come around often, you know.

402
00:31:05,120 --> 00:31:05,810
Here.

403
00:31:10,510 --> 00:31:12,000
Eat up. Come on.

404
00:31:20,730 --> 00:31:21,490
What?

405
00:31:23,370 --> 00:31:24,950
I think you need to change your shirt.

406
00:31:25,080 --> 00:31:26,310
I brought a spare one.

407
00:31:26,540 --> 00:31:29,290
See? I've literally brought you everything.

408
00:31:33,090 --> 00:31:33,800
P'Ing...

409
00:31:34,640 --> 00:31:35,440
What?

410
00:31:36,010 --> 00:31:37,210
Are you hurt?

411
00:31:37,230 --> 00:31:38,280
I'm not.

412
00:31:38,310 --> 00:31:39,480
You should worry about yourself.

413
00:31:39,550 --> 00:31:41,270
Damn, just eat this.

414
00:31:41,750 --> 00:31:42,570
P'Ing,

415
00:31:42,910 --> 00:31:43,980
your arm...

416
00:31:44,410 --> 00:31:45,180
What's wrong with it?

417
00:31:45,600 --> 00:31:47,670
Wait, that is my blood.

418
00:31:50,500 --> 00:31:53,180
You should take off your shirt so I can treat the wound.

419
00:31:53,400 --> 00:31:54,970
Damn, is it bad?

420
00:31:55,740 --> 00:31:57,800
It's probably nothing. Just a small scratch.

421
00:31:59,170 --> 00:32:00,580
Check my arm.

422
00:32:03,870 --> 00:32:04,910
Are there many wounds?

423
00:32:08,940 --> 00:32:10,280
-P'Ing. -What?

424
00:32:10,820 --> 00:32:11,650
Your back.

425
00:32:11,670 --> 00:32:12,350
My back?

426
00:32:12,900 --> 00:32:13,700
Oh...

427
00:32:14,430 --> 00:32:15,120
Damn it.

428
00:32:15,240 --> 00:32:16,090
God...

429
00:32:16,570 --> 00:32:17,370
I think...

430
00:32:18,430 --> 00:32:19,230
Ow.

431
00:32:20,230 --> 00:32:21,080
Jeez.

432
00:32:21,530 --> 00:32:24,990
Something must have slashed my back while I was running.

433
00:32:25,280 --> 00:32:26,750
Stay still.

434
00:32:26,780 --> 00:32:27,690
Damn.

435
00:32:28,540 --> 00:32:30,550
Dammit, what is this?

436
00:32:40,000 --> 00:32:41,200
Hey, be gentle.

437
00:32:46,270 --> 00:32:47,070
Easy does it.

438
00:32:48,790 --> 00:32:49,890
Stay still.

439
00:32:53,310 --> 00:32:53,920
Ow.

440
00:32:54,670 --> 00:32:56,620
It hurts like hell.

441
00:32:56,720 --> 00:32:58,180
Be more gentle, damn it.

442
00:32:58,900 --> 00:33:00,760
I don't know how to do this, either.

443
00:33:01,760 --> 00:33:03,420
I shouldn't have given you a hard time.

444
00:33:03,440 --> 00:33:05,000
Damn...

445
00:33:08,820 --> 00:33:09,950
Just bear with it.

446
00:33:15,650 --> 00:33:18,420
Yok, be gentle.

447
00:33:25,210 --> 00:33:26,800
Come on, move closer.

448
00:33:33,360 --> 00:33:34,350
You should get some sleep.

449
00:33:35,750 --> 00:33:37,350
If the weather clears up tomorrow,

450
00:33:38,580 --> 00:33:40,050
someone will eventually come for us.

451
00:33:47,720 --> 00:33:48,570
P'Ing...

452
00:33:49,610 --> 00:33:52,160
I didn't think you'd actually come for me.

453
00:33:55,380 --> 00:33:56,480
To be honest,

454
00:33:58,370 --> 00:33:59,920
if you hadn't been getting on my nerves,

455
00:34:00,740 --> 00:34:02,190
I might have gotten here even sooner.

456
00:34:08,590 --> 00:34:09,880
Why are you staring at me?

457
00:34:11,909 --> 00:34:13,510
Are you moved by my heroics?

458
00:34:18,219 --> 00:34:20,199
Fine, I'll stop teasing you.

459
00:34:23,280 --> 00:34:27,389
♪ You're the hush after rain ♪

460
00:34:27,420 --> 00:34:30,900
♪ A calm that I can't name ♪

461
00:34:30,920 --> 00:34:34,060
♪ Not a storm, just a glow ♪

462
00:34:34,520 --> 00:34:37,320
♪ Where my restless heart goes ♪

463
00:34:37,350 --> 00:34:41,449
♪ Never dreamed I'd love you this much ♪

464
00:34:41,480 --> 00:34:44,870
♪ There's nothing more to say about us ♪

465
00:34:44,900 --> 00:34:47,929
♪ You're the answer I never asked ♪

466
00:34:47,949 --> 00:34:51,989
♪ Without a doubt, this love will last ♪

467
00:34:52,020 --> 00:34:53,020
Do you think...

468
00:34:55,900 --> 00:34:57,690
we're going to make it through tonight?

469
00:34:58,860 --> 00:35:00,140
Watch your mouth.

470
00:35:00,390 --> 00:35:01,820
Don't jinx us.

471
00:35:10,590 --> 00:35:11,470
Here.

472
00:35:12,820 --> 00:35:13,820
What's this?

473
00:35:15,000 --> 00:35:15,870
A necklace.

474
00:35:23,940 --> 00:35:25,100
My mom gave it to me.

475
00:35:25,910 --> 00:35:27,750
My name, "Tiwakorn,"

476
00:35:28,140 --> 00:35:29,250
means the sun.

477
00:35:34,300 --> 00:35:35,570
I'm giving it to you,

478
00:35:36,640 --> 00:35:39,380
so you have to watch the sunrise with me tomorrow.

479
00:35:39,400 --> 00:35:40,380
Got it?

480
00:35:45,990 --> 00:35:47,100
P'Ing.

481
00:35:47,260 --> 00:35:48,060
Yeah?

482
00:35:51,330 --> 00:35:53,140
If we make it through tonight,

483
00:35:54,410 --> 00:35:55,860
will you be my boyfriend?

484
00:36:00,270 --> 00:36:01,860
Seriously, so you're just now realizing

485
00:36:01,880 --> 00:36:02,610
how great I am?

486
00:36:08,320 --> 00:36:09,450
Go to sleep now.

487
00:36:10,010 --> 00:36:12,080
Someone will come for us tomorrow

488
00:36:13,450 --> 00:36:14,800
after the storm dies down.

489
00:36:15,570 --> 00:36:16,520
Get some sleep.

490
00:36:17,420 --> 00:36:18,970
Take good care of my mom's necklace.

491
00:36:19,000 --> 00:36:20,890
If you lose it, you're dead.

492
00:36:21,290 --> 00:36:25,300
♪ Never dreamed I'd love you this much ♪

493
00:36:25,320 --> 00:36:28,900
♪ There's nothing more to say about us ♪

494
00:36:28,920 --> 00:36:31,810
♪ You're the answer I never asked ♪

495
00:36:31,830 --> 00:36:36,770
♪ The crack I didn't know I had ♪

496
00:36:39,030 --> 00:36:47,110
♪ Until I found you ♪

497
00:37:40,930 --> 00:37:41,910
P'Ing,

498
00:37:42,520 --> 00:37:43,850
the rain has stopped.

499
00:37:52,120 --> 00:37:52,920
P'Ing,

500
00:37:53,610 --> 00:37:55,080
the sun is coming out.

501
00:38:01,380 --> 00:38:02,300
P'Ing?

502
00:38:03,110 --> 00:38:04,050
Hey.

503
00:38:04,890 --> 00:38:05,730
P'Ing...

504
00:38:13,310 --> 00:38:15,340
You said we'd watch the sunrise together, didn't you?

505
00:38:16,260 --> 00:38:18,290
P'Ing...

506
00:38:18,570 --> 00:38:20,500
P'Ing.

507
00:38:38,460 --> 00:38:40,400
Oh, you're finally awake.

508
00:38:40,460 --> 00:38:41,740
Here is your phone, sir.

509
00:38:41,760 --> 00:38:43,360
I've already charged it for you.

510
00:38:43,410 --> 00:38:45,110
I'll leave it right here.

511
00:38:46,590 --> 00:38:47,550
The rescue team brought you

512
00:38:47,570 --> 00:38:49,740
and another gentleman in.

513
00:38:49,970 --> 00:38:52,200
You were unconscious for several hours.

514
00:38:52,220 --> 00:38:54,580
How is that gentleman who was with me?

515
00:38:55,460 --> 00:38:57,560
The doctor gave him a fever reducer,

516
00:38:57,590 --> 00:38:58,930
but he hasn't woken up yet.

517
00:38:59,070 --> 00:39:01,750
He's being monitored in the room right next door.

518
00:39:05,150 --> 00:39:06,640
Don't try to move yet.

519
00:39:06,990 --> 00:39:08,130
You're still on an IV drip.

520
00:39:08,170 --> 00:39:10,150
The doctor said you need plenty of rest.

521
00:39:10,180 --> 00:39:10,900
Okay.

522
00:39:12,900 --> 00:39:13,990
Please get some rest.

523
00:39:50,120 --> 00:39:51,310
Sweetie...

524
00:39:54,340 --> 00:39:55,590
Have you eaten yet?

525
00:39:57,350 --> 00:39:58,750
I'll go get your medicine.

526
00:39:59,000 --> 00:40:00,760
Eat something so you can take your meds, okay?

527
00:40:54,720 --> 00:40:55,520
P'Ing?

528
00:40:57,530 --> 00:40:59,110
What the hell is going on?

529
00:41:00,350 --> 00:41:01,470
Don't tell me...

530
00:41:03,820 --> 00:41:04,850
you've been holding me

531
00:41:04,880 --> 00:41:06,800
since we were rushed here.

532
00:41:09,070 --> 00:41:09,990
I haven't.

533
00:41:11,540 --> 00:41:14,840
Then why are you clinging to me like this?

534
00:41:14,910 --> 00:41:16,930
Is there a shortage of hospital beds?

535
00:41:17,690 --> 00:41:18,850
That's not it, either.

536
00:41:19,160 --> 00:41:20,370
I see.

537
00:41:21,070 --> 00:41:24,390
You must have just been waiting...

538
00:41:24,420 --> 00:41:26,460
for the chance to cuddle up with me in bed.

539
00:41:29,240 --> 00:41:30,040
P'Ing,

540
00:41:32,760 --> 00:41:34,490
about what I said yesterday...

541
00:41:34,750 --> 00:41:36,220
You mean about last night?

542
00:41:38,900 --> 00:41:40,890
What about it? I don't seem to remember.

543
00:41:44,850 --> 00:41:46,350
Are you going back on your word?

544
00:41:56,580 --> 00:41:58,880
I'll marry into your family.

545
00:41:59,180 --> 00:42:00,050
As for you,

546
00:42:00,080 --> 00:42:01,760
you have to be my bottom, though.

547
00:42:01,780 --> 00:42:03,170
This is actually nice.

548
00:42:03,190 --> 00:42:03,700
P'Ing.

549
00:42:03,720 --> 00:42:05,720
When something good happens to you,

550
00:42:05,750 --> 00:42:07,340
it's natural to look radiant.

551
00:42:07,370 --> 00:42:09,020
It's about that tryout at the boxing gym.

552
00:42:09,050 --> 00:42:10,300
They want to sign me to a contract

553
00:42:10,330 --> 00:42:11,920
and have me train in America.

554
00:42:12,150 --> 00:42:13,830
But there's some good news.

555
00:42:14,000 --> 00:42:15,130
I know him better than anyone.

556
00:42:15,150 --> 00:42:16,110
My brother...

557
00:42:16,130 --> 00:42:17,510
hates nothing more than being lied to.

558
00:42:17,870 --> 00:42:19,620
The second you helped me,

559
00:42:19,640 --> 00:42:20,580
you'd already betrayed him.

560
00:42:20,590 --> 00:42:21,300
Itt...

561
00:42:22,330 --> 00:42:24,440
Are we still friends?
